<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syrym Datuly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1802</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Srym Datov</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syrym Datuly was a Kazakh batyr of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baiuly">Baiuly</a> tribes of the Junior Zhuz who led a revolt from 1783 to 1797 against Russian colonial pressure and the khans who cooperated with it. His forces raided Russian forts along the Ural line and helped drive out Khan Nurali. He later fled south and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> in 1802.</p></div>
